<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out as of 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out as of 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as of 3:00 PM, boxed beef values were uneven on moderate to fairly good demand and mostly moderate offerings. Select and Choice rib and chuck cuts were firm, round cuts weak, loin cuts uneven. Beef trimmings were steady on light to moderate demand/offers.- USDA</p>
<p> 304 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>  74 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>39 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     107.27	105.79	101.96	100.86</p>
<p>		    0.86	  0.30	  0.69	 -0.02</p>
<p>	     CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>Rib	  153.46	151.65	140.24	139.64</p>
<p>Chuck	 82.27	 77.81	 81.51	 77.00</p>
<p>Round	109.46	109.46	105.27	105.27</p>
<p>Loin	 148.83	148.97	136.11	137.50</p>
<p>Brisket     58.28	 58.28	 57.99	 57.99</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  66.04	 65.98	 66.22	 66.09</p>
<p>Flank	 66.80	 66.80	 66.85	 66.85</p>
